# Dashboard

Give your team one place to check progress, review recent activity, and act on orders.

## When to use
The landing page of an app or workspace that summarizes what changed. Not a place for editing: link to the list or detail pages instead.

## What to replace
- The workspace name and the avatar in the top bar.
- `stats`, `activity` and `orders` with your data, and the card titles.
- The chart sketch with your chart. Keep one text alternative that states what the chart shows.

## How to adapt
- Every card title is an h2; add or remove cards without breaking the outline.
- Stat cards fill the row automatically; cards with `dashboard__wide` take the full row.
- While loading, keep the cards in place with skeletons, set `aria-busy` on the panel and show one labelled spinner by the h1.
- Change layout in `dashboard.css` only, with semantic tokens.
